{
  "artifact_id": "evidence-combined-sqsp-permira-artifact-slice-049052fee9",
  "artifact_type": "evidence_bundle",
  "child_artifact_ids": [],
  "claim_records": [
    {
      "citation_ids": [],
      "claim_id": "CLM-001",
      "confidence": 0.35,
      "original_claim_id": "CLM-001",
      "quality_flags": [
        "missing_citation"
      ],
      "report_artifact_id": "report-sqsp-permira-artifact-slice-3d571b69b4",
      "section_id": "section_002",
      "text": "Assess whether Squarespace's post-take-private growth base is strong enough for a PE sponsor to underwrite value creation without relying mainly on multiple expansion."
    },
    {
      "citation_ids": [
        "SRC-001"
      ],
      "claim_id": "CLM-002",
      "confidence": 0.55,
      "original_claim_id": "CLM-002",
      "quality_flags": [],
      "report_artifact_id": "report-sqsp-permira-artifact-slice-3d571b69b4",
      "section_id": "section_003",
      "text": "Permira completed the acquisition of Squarespace on October 17, 2024, and the transaction valued the company at approximately $7.2 billion, so the diligence question is now a sponsor-owned value-creation question rather than a public-shareholder voting question."
    },
    {
      "citation_ids": [
        "SRC-002"
      ],
      "claim_id": "CLM-003",
      "confidence": 0.55,
      "original_claim_id": "CLM-003",
      "quality_flags": [],
      "report_artifact_id": "report-sqsp-permira-artifact-slice-3d571b69b4",
      "section_id": "section_003",
      "text": "Squarespace's Q2 2024 total revenue was $296.8 million, up 20% year over year, which indicates the company entered the take-private with real top-line momentum rather than a stalled revenue base."
    },
    {
      "citation_ids": [
        "SRC-002"
      ],
      "claim_id": "CLM-004",
      "confidence": 0.55,
      "original_claim_id": "CLM-004",
      "quality_flags": [],
      "report_artifact_id": "report-sqsp-permira-artifact-slice-3d571b69b4",
      "section_id": "section_003",
      "text": "Annual run-rate revenue reached $1.179 billion in Q2 2024, up 20% year over year, while unique subscriptions increased 21% to more than 5.2 million, giving the sponsor a large subscription base to monetize."
    },
    {
      "citation_ids": [
        "SRC-002"
      ],
      "claim_id": "CLM-005",
      "confidence": 0.55,
      "original_claim_id": "CLM-005",
      "quality_flags": [],
      "report_artifact_id": "report-sqsp-permira-artifact-slice-3d571b69b4",
      "section_id": "section_003",
      "text": "Average revenue per unique subscription rose only 3% year over year to $225.45, which suggests that near-term value creation probably needs price-packaging, attachment, or mix improvements in addition to continued subscription growth."
    },
    {
      "citation_ids": [
        "SRC-002"
      ],
      "claim_id": "CLM-006",
      "confidence": 0.55,
      "original_claim_id": "CLM-006",
      "quality_flags": [],
      "report_artifact_id": "report-sqsp-permira-artifact-slice-3d571b69b4",
      "section_id": "section_003",
      "text": "Squarespace's own metric definition says ARRR is a run-rate indicator and not a GAAP revenue forecast, so underwriting should avoid treating ARRR as guaranteed next-year revenue."
    },
    {
      "citation_ids": [
        "SRC-003"
      ],
      "claim_id": "CLM-007",
      "confidence": 0.55,
      "original_claim_id": "CLM-007",
      "quality_flags": [],
      "report_artifact_id": "report-sqsp-permira-artifact-slice-3d571b69b4",
      "section_id": "section_003",
      "text": "Wix reported Q2 2024 bookings of $458.4 million, up 15% year over year, and attributed momentum partly to Wix Studio, AI capabilities, and commerce expansion, creating a competitive benchmark that Squarespace must answer with product depth and partner-led growth rather than brand alone."
    },
    {
      "citation_ids": [
        "SRC-004"
      ],
      "claim_id": "CLM-008",
      "confidence": 0.55,
      "original_claim_id": "CLM-008",
      "quality_flags": [],
      "report_artifact_id": "report-sqsp-permira-artifact-slice-3d571b69b4",
      "section_id": "section_003",
      "text": "The merger announcement warned of business disruption, employee-retention, financing, regulatory, and competitive-response risks, making continuity and execution quality explicit diligence gates after close."
    },
    {
      "citation_ids": [],
      "claim_id": "CLM-009",
      "confidence": 0.35,
      "original_claim_id": "CLM-009",
      "quality_flags": [
        "missing_citation"
      ],
      "report_artifact_id": "report-sqsp-permira-artifact-slice-3d571b69b4",
      "section_id": "section_004",
      "text": "The growth branch is directionally attractive but not self-proving."
    },
    {
      "citation_ids": [],
      "claim_id": "CLM-010",
      "confidence": 0.35,
      "original_claim_id": "CLM-010",
      "quality_flags": [
        "missing_citation"
      ],
      "report_artifact_id": "report-sqsp-permira-artifact-slice-3d571b69b4",
      "section_id": "section_004",
      "text": "Subscription count and ARRR growth support further diligence, while modest ARPUS growth and Wix's stronger agency/Studio narrative imply that sponsor upside needs a focused monetization and product-extension plan."
    },
    {
      "citation_ids": [],
      "claim_id": "CLM-011",
      "confidence": 0.35,
      "original_claim_id": "CLM-011",
      "quality_flags": [
        "missing_citation"
      ],
      "report_artifact_id": "report-sqsp-permira-artifact-slice-3d571b69b4",
      "section_id": "section_004",
      "text": "The most important disconfirming evidence would be cohort-level data showing that incremental subscriptions came from lower-quality Google Domains migration effects or low-retention price-sensitive customers."
    },
    {
      "citation_ids": [],
      "claim_id": "CLM-012",
      "confidence": 0.35,
      "original_claim_id": "CLM-001",
      "quality_flags": [
        "missing_citation"
      ],
      "report_artifact_id": "report-sqsp-permira-artifact-slice-8e174fe880",
      "section_id": "section_002",
      "text": "Assess whether Squarespace's margin, cash-flow, and portfolio posture can support private-equity value creation after the Permira take-private."
    },
    {
      "citation_ids": [
        "SRC-005"
      ],
      "claim_id": "CLM-013",
      "confidence": 0.55,
      "original_claim_id": "CLM-002",
      "quality_flags": [],
      "report_artifact_id": "report-sqsp-permira-artifact-slice-8e174fe880",
      "section_id": "section_003",
      "text": "Squarespace generated $72.1 million of adjusted EBITDA in Q2 2024 against $296.8 million of revenue, but adjusted EBITDA declined slightly year over year, so growth was not translating into automatic EBITDA expansion at the latest public checkpoint."
    },
    {
      "citation_ids": [
        "SRC-005"
      ],
      "claim_id": "CLM-014",
      "confidence": 0.55,
      "original_claim_id": "CLM-003",
      "quality_flags": [],
      "report_artifact_id": "report-sqsp-permira-artifact-slice-8e174fe880",
      "section_id": "section_003",
      "text": "Unlevered free cash flow was $65.4 million in Q2 2024 and $154.7 million for the first half of 2024, giving the sponsor a cash-generative asset base for deleveraging, reinvestment, or tuck-in work."
    },
    {
      "citation_ids": [
        "SRC-005"
      ],
      "claim_id": "CLM-015",
      "confidence": 0.55,
      "original_claim_id": "CLM-004",
      "quality_flags": [],
      "report_artifact_id": "report-sqsp-permira-artifact-slice-8e174fe880",
      "section_id": "section_003",
      "text": "Net cash provided by operating activities was $145.8 million for the first half of 2024 versus $116.7 million in the prior-year period, supporting the view that the company had improving cash conversion before delisting."
    },
    {
      "citation_ids": [
        "SRC-005"
      ],
      "claim_id": "CLM-016",
      "confidence": 0.55,
      "original_claim_id": "CLM-005",
      "quality_flags": [],
      "report_artifact_id": "report-sqsp-permira-artifact-slice-8e174fe880",
      "section_id": "section_003",
      "text": "Squarespace's Q2 2024 disclosure warns that adjusted EBITDA and unlevered free cash flow are non-GAAP measures and should be used only alongside GAAP results, so diligence should reconcile reported non-GAAP cash generation to debt capacity and sponsor-case liquidity."
    },
    {
      "citation_ids": [
        "SRC-006"
      ],
      "claim_id": "CLM-017",
      "confidence": 0.55,
      "original_claim_id": "CLM-006",
      "quality_flags": [],
      "report_artifact_id": "report-sqsp-permira-artifact-slice-8e174fe880",
      "section_id": "section_003",
      "text": "Squarespace agreed in June 2024 to sell Tock to American Express for $400 million in cash, creating a portfolio-simplification and liquidity event that can sharpen focus on the core website, domains, commerce, and entrepreneur platform."
    },
    {
      "citation_ids": [
        "SRC-007"
      ],
      "claim_id": "CLM-018",
      "confidence": 0.55,
      "original_claim_id": "CLM-007",
      "quality_flags": [],
      "report_artifact_id": "report-sqsp-permira-artifact-slice-8e174fe880",
      "section_id": "section_003",
      "text": "American Express completed the Tock acquisition on October 15, 2024, removing a non-core hospitality platform from the Squarespace perimeter immediately before the Permira closing."
    },
    {
      "citation_ids": [
        "SRC-008"
      ],
      "claim_id": "CLM-019",
      "confidence": 0.55,
      "original_claim_id": "CLM-008",
      "quality_flags": [],
      "report_artifact_id": "report-sqsp-permira-artifact-slice-8e174fe880",
      "section_id": "section_003",
      "text": "The transaction announcement's risk factors include financing, rating-agency, macro, litigation, disruption, and employee-retention risks, so the cash-flow branch should include downside cases for debt cost, retention, and execution disruption rather than assuming a frictionless take-private."
    },
    {
      "citation_ids": [],
      "claim_id": "CLM-020",
      "confidence": 0.35,
      "original_claim_id": "CLM-009",
      "quality_flags": [
        "missing_citation"
      ],
      "report_artifact_id": "report-sqsp-permira-artifact-slice-8e174fe880",
      "section_id": "section_004",
      "text": "The margin and cash-flow branch supports proceeding to deeper diligence, with a caution."
    },
    {
      "citation_ids": [],
      "claim_id": "CLM-021",
      "confidence": 0.35,
      "original_claim_id": "CLM-010",
      "quality_flags": [
        "missing_citation"
      ],
      "report_artifact_id": "report-sqsp-permira-artifact-slice-8e174fe880",
      "section_id": "section_004",
      "text": "Squarespace had meaningful unlevered free cash flow and a cleaner portfolio after Tock, but the public checkpoint did not show clear EBITDA expansion."
    },
    {
      "citation_ids": [],
      "claim_id": "CLM-022",
      "confidence": 0.35,
      "original_claim_id": "CLM-011",
      "quality_flags": [
        "missing_citation"
      ],
      "report_artifact_id": "report-sqsp-permira-artifact-slice-8e174fe880",
      "section_id": "section_004",
      "text": "The next analytical artifact should be a sponsor-case bridge that separates recurring subscription gross margin, operating expense leverage, Google Domains integration effects, post-Tock perimeter changes, debt service, and reinvestment needs."
    }
  ],
